# Lost Island

Lost Island is a 3D action-adventure prototype built in Godot 4.

The project is currently focused on a small playable demo used to develop
the core character, combat, elemental skill, progression, and menu systems.

## Current Features

- Third-person character movement
- Running and stamina
- Jumping
- Physical weapon attacks
- Elemental skill selection
- Mana-based skills
- Slow-motion weapon/element selection
- Health, stamina, mana, and loadout HUD
- Character menu
- Inventory page
- Settings page
- Character stat display with equipment bonuses
- Skill tree interface
- Skill-point progression
- Unlockable Fire skills
- Menu character preview

## Current Elements

### Physical

Uses stamina and the currently equipped weapon.

### Fire

Fire skill tree and progression are currently the most developed elemental
systems.

### Water

Basic skill support exists. A full Water skill tree is not yet implemented.

### Light

Basic skill support exists. A full Light skill tree is not yet implemented.

## Architecture

### Player

`Scripts/Player/player.gd`

Responsible for:

- Player input
- Movement
- Jumping
- Combat input
- Element selection
- Weapon-wheel state
- Global slow motion

### PlayerCharacter

`Scripts/Player/player_character.gd`

Responsible for:

- Runtime character stats
- Health
- Stamina
- Mana
- Equipment
- Skill costs
- Skill effects
- Combat animations

### PlayerProgress

`Scripts/Player/player_progress.gd`

Responsible for:

- Skill points
- Unlocked skill IDs
- Skill-purchase validation

### PlayerHUD

`Scripts/UI/player_ui.gd`

Gameplay HUD driven primarily through PlayerCharacter signals.

### MenuUI

`Scripts/UI/menu_ui.gd`

Controls the Character, Inventory, Settings, and Skill Tree interfaces.

### Skills

`Scripts/Skills/skills.gd`

Resource definition for individual skills.

Skills contain identity, progression cost, gameplay data, resource cost,
animation information, and regeneration effects.

### Skillbook

`Scripts/Skills/skillbook.gd`

Stores the currently available combat skills for each elemental type.

### SkillTree / SkillTreeNode

Reusable UI controllers used to display and interact with elemental
skill trees.

### Stats / StatModifiers

`Stats` contains character stat values.

`StatModifiers` contains additive equipment bonuses and is kept separate
from base character stats.

### StateManager

`Scripts/Core/state_manager.gd`

Global game-state manager.

Current states:

- TITLE
- PLAY
- MENU
- WEAPON

## Development Direction

The character is not intended to choose a permanent class.

Instead, character identity will emerge from:

- Equipment
- Unlocked skills
- Element investment
- Stat distribution
- Skill loadout

Future character titles may recognize those builds without defining them.

Example:

- Fire-focused build -> Pyromancer
- Physical-heavy build -> Vanguard
- Fire + Physical -> Ember Knight

The build determines the title; the title does not determine the build.

## Planned Systems

- Skill loadout assignment
- Additional elemental skill trees
- Save/load persistence
- Weapon damage and hit detection
- Enemy combat
- Skill-tree prerequisites
- Derived character titles
- Additional equipment
- Demo-world content

## Development Status

This is an active prototype and not a finished game.
